@title  PCSA00002 - boot, walk the front end, and reach a LIVE GAME
@game   PCSA00002
@shot-every 200

# WHAT THIS RECIPE IS FOR
# ----------------------
# The GAMEPLAY recipe for this title. `boot-user-settings.recipe` beside it stops at the
# first interactive screen and exercises only the boot path; this one carries on through
# the title screen, the mode list and the stadium options and arrives at a LIVE GAME.
#
# LIVE GAMEPLAY IS FRAMES 11700-11800. The frame at f011800 is a wide shot of the field
# with the batter up: 8 scenes / ~681 draws, the world pass, the three 128x128 probe
# atlases, the jumbotron boards and the HUD. That is the frame every render question about
# this title is asked at, so keep it reachable.
#
# HOW THE TITLE SCREEN IS DISMISSED, because it is not a button
# -------------------------------------------------------------
# This title's title screen wants a TOUCH, not a press, and it does not say where. The
# sweep at 2200-2356 walks a row of touch points across y=560 in both directions, which
# hits whatever the live rectangle is without anyone having to know it. Do not "tidy" it
# into a single touch: the coordinates have never been confirmed, and a single point that
# misses leaves the run sitting on the title screen with a plausible-looking log.
#
# RUNNING IT WITHOUT PAYING FOR 11,810 RENDERED FRAMES
# ---------------------------------------------------
# Rendering is what costs. `VITASLOP_HEADLESS_SHOT_FROM/TO` bound the window that is
# rendered at all, so
#
#   VITASLOP_HEADLESS_FRAMES=11810 SHOT_FROM=11700 SHOT_TO=11800 SHOT_EVERY=20
#
# is about a minute against fifteen, and the composition at f011800 is IDENTICAL to the
# full replay's. What a narrow window CAN change is a target painted once long before it
# and sampled during it - so read a picture from a windowed run against ANOTHER windowed
# run, never against a full replay. `working-area/mlbfast.sh` is that rig.
#
# There is deliberately no @sig: this has never been run twice on one build to see whether
# it folds the same number, and a pinned signature nobody has confirmed is a test that
# fails for the wrong reason.

